# A 2-D rampart: a tanh cliff 900 m high on 200 m cells (README.md has the case). 80 x 2 x 60 cells over
# 16 km x 400 m, y periodic, the layers from mesh.dz0 by a fixed ratio to a top at 10 km. The wind climbs the cliff:
# a log law over the sea (u* = 0.3031 m/s, z0 = 0.0002 m) on xlo, outflow on the plateau; a no-slip lid
# moving at the log-law speed of the top (13.107 m/s); Rayleigh damping of w above 8 km; neutral, no Coriolis.
# The recommended closure setting and a steep-terrain solver setting (line LU-SGS, two sweeps, CFL cap 16, the w rows'
# VNN cap 16).
# Command line: terrain.file (rampart_steep.xyz or rampart_gentle.xyz, from make_terrain.py), mesh.dz0 and
# mesh.stretch_ratio (2 and 1.111114, or 8 and 1.079941), steady.max_iterations.
mesh.n_cell        = 80 2 60
mesh.prob_lo       = 0. 0. 0.
mesh.prob_hi       = 16000. 400. 10000.
mesh.is_periodic   = 0 1 0
mesh.max_grid_size = 40 2

terrain.type      = xyz
terrain.smoothing = 0

bc.xlo = inflow
bc.xhi = outflow
bc.zlo = surface_layer
bc.zhi = no_slip_wall
bc.zhi_wall_velocity = 13.107 0. 0.
bc.surface_z0       = 0.0002
bc.inflow_profile   = log_law
bc.inflow_ustar     = 0.3031
bc.inflow_z0        = 0.0002
bc.inflow_direction = 0.
bc.theta_profile_z  = 0.
bc.theta_profile    = 300.
bc.rayleigh_zdamp    = 8000.
bc.rayleigh_dampcoef = 0.2
bc.rayleigh_fields   = w

forcing.gravity  = 0.
turb.tke_floor   = 1.e-6
turb.realizability = 0.309
turb.nut_relax     = 0.5
convection.hybrid_sigma_max = 0.1
convection.hybrid_height    = 7600.
turb.max_geom_lscale = 1.e6
simplec.w_vnn_cap = 16

init.first_guess = profile

steady.stage        = simplec
steady.sweep        = lusgs
steady.zline_sweeps = 2
steady.cfl_max      = 16

io.plot_file = rampart_plt
io.write_plotfile   = 0
io.write_checkpoint = 0
